---
title: PyCascades 2020 Dates, Location, & CFP
---
author: PyCascades Team
---
date: 2019-08-21
---
meta_description: PyCascades 2020 will take place on February 8th & 9th, 2020
---
body:

We have lots of announcements to share about PyCascades 2020. 🎉🎉🎉

Dates & Location
-----------------

PyCascades 2020 will take place on **Saturday, February 8th & Sunday, February 9th** at `Revolution Hall <https://www.revolutionhall.com>`__ in Portland, Oregon.
We'll also have our community sprints at Revolution Hall on **Monday, February 9th** as well as a pre-conference social on **Friday, February 7th**.
We'll have more details about the venue, including accessibility information, in the coming months.
If you have questions or concerns in the meantime please reach out to us at organizers@pycascades.com.

Tickets
--------

We're not quite ready to start selling tickets yet. We'll have another announcement for that coming soon.
Subscribe to our `newsletter </#newsletter>`__ to be the first to know (it's only important stuff, we promise)!

Call for Proposals
-------------------

PyCascades has been lucky to give our stage to incredible speakers with wonderful talks over the last two years.
We are really looking forward to showcasing our community again next year.
Our `Call for Proposals (CFP) <https://todo>`__ opens today and closes on **Tuesday, October 1st, 2019**.

Considering speaking at PyCascades? Great! We're looking forward to reading your proposal!

Never considered speaking at PyCascades? We think you should! We love proposals from:

- People who've never spoken before (we've got mentors for you)!
- People new to Python.
- People who use Python in their spare time.
- People who want to talk about something that isn't specifically Python. 

What gets your excited? What cool art did you build? What's something you wish someone had told you years ago? What interesting problem have you solved recently?
Talks can be about anything that someone in the Python community would be interested in hearing about. 

If you're interested please take a look at the instructions on `PaperCall <https://todo>`__.

If you need financial assistance to speak or attend PyCascades we will be continuing our opportunity grants program this year. We'll have more details soon but feel free to reach out to organizers@pycascades.com in the meantime.

Call for Organizers
--------------------

Are you interesting in helping organize PyCascades?
We're looking for volunteers to take on the these roles:

- Financial Aid Chair: Responsible for our opportunity grants program.
- Volunteer Coordinator: Responsible for finding, organizing, and overseeing volunteers.
- Communications Chair: Responsible for writing and reviewing all PyCascades communications and maintaining the PyCascades website.